escribe candidate-view publication, overlapping chat lines 78–101. Final diagrams/generated and diagram_generation/gate both expand submission mechanics; canvas_commands/views lines 13–20 and chat/isolate lines 22–25 both explain candidate publication. Within parsing, seed lines 17–26 become closely repeated material in central lines 13–18 and folding lines 2–9.","impact":"The collection repeatedly restarts explanations of shared mechanisms. Some repetition provides necessary local context, but the seeds do not consistently distinguish a point’s owned explanation from a short dependency contract. The later stage adds its own central/peripheral duplication, amplifying this ambiguity rather than originating all of it.","recommendation":"Assign shared mechanisms a clear explanatory home while retaining brief, locally useful summaries elsewhere. Let diagrams own revision and continuity semantics, diagram_generation own orchestration and installation, canvas_commands own saved-view behavior, and chat own candidate conversation coordination. Make secondary mentions state what is consumed or invoked and where the deeper explanation belongs. Do not remove repetition that explains a genuinely different consequence."},{"evidence":"An end-to-end publication chain is distributed across rendering seed line 34 ('controller.commitEditorGesture'), canvas_commands line 18 ('historyService.append -> publish controller snapshot'), workspace lines 33 and 55–72 (persistence notification and delivery), and persistence lines 38–52 (blob/manifest publication). chat explicitly references [agent_access], [contexts], and [canvas_commands] at lines 39, 79, and 88, but comparable handoffs elsewhere are usually implicit. Final rendering and canvas_commands edges predominantly connect central concepts to explanatory peripherals; workspace additionally connects session to records and records to delivery.","impact":"Individual trees explain their components, but readers must reconstruct how the collection’s components cooperate. A tree branch may organize a topic, list owned state, or describe execution; those meanings are often carried only by local wording. Most final edges then express elaboration rather than the system relationships spanning points. Actual cross-canvas navigation is a later responsibility, but clearer handoffs could have been supplied by Phase 2.","recommendation":"Name important producer/consumer handoffs in the seeds using consistent component names and explicit verbs. For the publication chain, identify the semantic commit, emitted checkpoint changes, delivery acknowledgement, and manifest visibility boundary at their respective owners. Use cross-point references where they resolve a real dependency. Preserve hierarchical grouping without implying that sibling order or indentation alone establishes execution or ownership."},{"evidence":"Several distinct identity scopes are locally described but not explicitly connected: diagrams seed lines 4–7 distinguish diagramId, revisionId, local Diagram.id, and parentId; line 17 constructs content with 'id:revision', while parsing line 22 calls the content-node prefix 'revisionId'. canvas_commands line 11 checks snapshot.version, workspace line 61 sends expectedRevision, persistence line 64 checks expectedRevisionId, and changes lines 15 and 23 discuss document and session versions. Final diagrams/identity lines 16–18 adds the important distinction between numeric content revision and immutable revision identity.","impact":"Repeated terms such as revision, version, and ID can appear interchangeable across otherwise detailed points. Readers can follow an individual check yet struggle to understand which identity survives an edit, which version guards a mutation, and which revision belongs to publication. This is a presentation ambiguity established by the labels, not an assertion that the underlying implementation confuses them.","recommendation":"Clarify identity scope at the relevant handoffs: local content key, logical diagram identity, immutable revision identity, parser/content identity, document version, session version, and storage/catalog revision where applicable. Explain conversions or bindings when they matter, using the existing owning points rather than repeating a universal glossary in every tree."},{"evidence":"agent_access seed line 23 says 'Mutations require current expectedVersion', whereas final agent_access/save lines 21–25 makes requirements operation-specific and identifies create/copy exceptions. changes seed lines 22–24 broadly groups version checks; final changes/edits lines 11–14 separates document-version, session-version, and unversioned creation. chat seed lines 116–118 describes disposal as interrupting chats and persisting/flushing; final chat/lifetime lines 16–20 instead distinguishes marking state, queued saves, and resources not removed there. composition seed line 122 says dependency direction is 'enforced', while final composition/rules lines 22–25 limits the evidence to test rules without execution results.","impact":"Broad seed wording turns local checks, cleanup calls, or intended rules into apparent guarantees. The final outputs spend substantial space narrowing these claims. Their reported corrections are output evidence, not independent source verification, but they demonstrate that the seed formulations did not preserve scope reliably. Qualification added later can also leave a stronger central summary beside a narrower peripheral explanation.","recommendation":"Regenerate guarantees with their operation and boundary attached. Distinguish invoking cleanup from completing it, queued persistence from acknowledged persistence, and a test’s policy from demonstrated enforcement. State version requirements for the relevant operation families instead of generalizing across all mutations. Carry uncertainty or delegated behavior compactly where it affects interpretation; avoid expanding every limitation into a separate audit narrative."}],"regenerationInstructions":"Regenerate the 15 seeds as a coordinated collection with distinct explanatory responsibilities. Preserve the successful separations among content, placement, live interaction, durable publication, pinned evidence, proposals, and evaluation. Reduce incidental mechanics where they obscure those boundaries; retain detail that explains a meaningful consequence or exception. Give shared mechanisms an explanatory home, keep concise dependency summaries elsewhere, and make important cross-point handoffs explicit. Clarify identity and version scopes and qualify guarantees at their actual boundary. Use grouping and relationship wording suited to each point, without a fixed template or branch count. Treat final-output refinements as evidence of presentation ambiguity to investigate, not as independently verified source facts. Final layout, peripheral counts, added implementation detail, and navigation remain later-phase responsibilities."}{"ascii":"Canvas Commands and History
|-- MappingDocumentController: shared mutation facade
|   |-- Entry points
|   |   |-- applyUpdate(expectedVersion, operations)
|   |   |   `-- transact delegates here for headless/API batches
|   |   |-- commitEditorGesture(operations, canvas)
|   |   |   `-- one native gesture includes selection/layout consequences in one checkpoint
|   |   `-- mounted canvas may attach one editor driver: settle + undo/redo
|   |-- Command publication path
|   |   |-- settle pending live gesture before applyUpdate
|   |   |-- require expectedVersion == snapshot.version
|   |   |   `-- mismatch -> VERSION_CONFLICT: read the canvas again
|   |   |-- clone document + canvas; apply operations sequentially
|   |   |   |-- API batch: 1..100 operations; native batch: up to 10000
|   |   |   |-- later operations see earlier staged edits
|   |   |   `-- operation-specific checks: IDs, revisions, content hashes and node anchors
|   |   |-- finish layout, reconcile links, prune orphan metadata and normalize selection/views
|   |   `-- validate -> historyService.append -> publish controller snapshot -> notify listeners
|   |       |-- validation failure prevents publication of the staged canvas checkpoint
|   |       `-- snapshot exposes version, checkpoint ID, canUndo and canRedo
|   |-- Operation families
|   |   |-- content: create, insert issued revision, patch, replace, apply revision
|   |   |-- composition: duplicate instance, move, group, collapse, remove, delete diagrams
|   |   |-- annotations: source mappings, jumps, highlights, presentation, agent context
|   |   |-- connections: edge-create, edge-update, edge-remove
|   |   `-- alternatives/reviews: store, select, review, apply and show side panels
|   `-- Transient selection/layout updates can avoid advancing history
|
|-- CanvasHistoryService: runtime ownership boundary
|   |-- controller holds a CanvasEditingContext handle
|   |-- DefaultCanvasHistoryService maps handle objects -> CanvasHistory in a WeakMap
|   |   `-- two viewers of the same persisted context remain isolated
|   |-- owns append, navigate, reset, fork, adopt, saved views and persistence access
|   `-- service and runtime handles are not saved in the canvas
|
|-- CanvasHistory: checkpoints bind composition to issued diagram revisions
|   |-- StoredCanvasSnapshot
|   |   |-- id + parentId + optional transfer transactionId
|   |   |-- document: placement tree, connections, sections, jumps and presentation metadata
|   |   |   `-- canonical scene stores root only; it does not embed diagram contents
|   |   |-- diagramBindings: content/diagram ID -> exact issued revision ID
|   |   |-- view: personal state restored separately from composition
|   |   `-- nodeOrigins + logical node references preserve correspondence across edits
|   |-- append(document, view, correspondence)
|   |   |-- validate scene, connections, jumps, contexts, settings and revision references
|   |   |-- assert issued diagrams; retain bound revisions and required dependencies
|   |   |   `-- also retain revisions used by alternatives, reviews and selections
|   |   |-- encode content anchors using revision nodeRefs
|   |   |   `-- already-stale endpoints remain explicitly unresolved
|   |   `-- publish checkpoint after validation completes
|   |       `-- previous head -> past; new checkpoint -> head; future -> empty
|   |-- documentFromHistory(checkpoint)
|   |   `-- bindings + revision table -> resolved contents + revision-specific anchors
|   |       `-- compatibility projection for rendering and transport; diagrams are frozen
|   |-- Navigation and branching
|   |   |-- undo: pop past -> head; previous head -> future
|   |   |-- redo: pop future -> head; previous head -> past
|   |   |-- edit after undo: append child of current head; clear redo route
|   |   |   `-- archived snapshots and revisions remain retained
|   |   |-- reset: copy baseline into a new checkpoint; reset itself is undoable
|   |   |-- fork: retain archive, create new context/baseline, clear past/future
|   |   |-- adopt: validate proposal, retain exact revision IDs, publish one new checkpoint
|   |   `-- live editor undo restores archived semantic checkpoints without creating edits
|   `-- Persistence and export
|       |-- persistenceChanges(since): navigation header + changed snapshots/revisions
|       |   `-- checkpoint encoder supplies storage records
|       |-- current-only export: real head ID + pinned dependencies + parent boundary IDs
|       `-- saved views or an active recording force full export to retain their graph
|
|-- LineGrid: reusable content and hierarchical placement are separate
|   |-- LineGridScene
|   |   |-- contents[contentId] -> reusable Diagram
|   |   `-- root -> GridBox tree
|   |       |-- diagram box -> contentId
|   |       |   `-- duplicate-instance adds a placement sharing the same content
|   |       `-- container -> children + push-right collision policy + gap
|   |-- Each box has relative cell position, collapse state and optional minimum size
|   |   |-- resolveScene accumulates absolute bounds from parent positions
|   |   `-- collapsed box displays collapsedContentId; hides children and ignores minimum size
|   |-- layoutScene(scene, changedId)
|   |   |-- anchor changed subtree at each ancestor
|   |   |-- settle siblings in stable spatial order, moving only right
|   |   `-- settled boxes become fixed obstacles; composeScene checks final bounds/collisions
|   `-- Geometry constraints
|       |-- printable ASCII + LF; zero-based cells; right/bottom edges exclusive
|       |-- coordinate/extent checks up to 20000; composition capped at 4000000 cells
|       `-- hitTest returns placement/content IDs and coordinates local to the hit box
|
|-- DiagramConnection: anchors depend on parsed content nodes
|   |-- source: content-node anchor; target: content-node or box anchor
|   |   `-- content anchor pins displayNodeId + contentNodeId + content revisionId
|   |-- create/update validates changed endpoints against current content
|   |   |-- missing placement or wrong node/revision -> reject
|   |   `-- unchanged endpoints may retain an already-stale revision
|   |-- reconcileConnections(before, after, edges, nodeIds)
|   |   |-- deleted endpoint placement -> remove incident edge
|   |   |-- proven node correspondence -> rebase node and revision IDs
|   |   |-- unchanged ASCII and structure kind -> match line/start-column position
|   |   `-- otherwise preserve stale anchor rather than guess a new endpoint
|   `-- patch/revision application also rebases supported jumps and collapse state
|       `-- patch line correspondence updates section ranges
|
|-- CanvasView: named saved states and branches owned by CanvasHistory
|   |-- saved metadata lives outside the state restored by undo/apply
|   |   `-- start/final checkpoint IDs, checkpoint sequence, parent/fork IDs and working copies
|   |-- create/save -> pin current state; saved checkpoints remain immutable
|   |-- open -> stash current working copy; resume target working copy or saved endpoint
|   |   `-- restore as a fresh checkpoint while retaining the current camera
|   |-- fork -> create and open child from parent's saved checkpoint
|   |-- alternatives -> create grouped children from ONE pinned saved checkpoint
|   |   `-- leaves active canvas unchanged; children are independent
|   |-- keep -> save candidate; archive group siblings and their descendants
|   |-- discard -> archive target and descendants; delete requires a leaf
|   |-- recording: start -> collect visited checkpoints -> stop saves endpoints
|   |   `-- cancel drops recording metadata while retaining edits
|   |-- comparison reads only pinned baseline/proposed endpoints and their dependencies
|   |-- dirty compares document, bindings and view state excluding viewport/selection
|   `-- generation
|       |-- startGeneration pins a saved parent state for candidate views
|       `-- finished proposal -> validate and retain revisions -> update candidate endpoint
|           `-- publication updates the saved candidate without switching the live head
|
`-- CanvasTransfer: prepare isolated histories; workspace owns publication
    |-- require another destination and a nonempty, unique selection of diagram placements
    |-- preserve relative placement; remap IDs, content, highlights and links as needed
    |-- copy
    |   |-- allocate fresh placement/content IDs; retain sharing within the copied selection
    |   |-- copy edges only when both endpoints are selected
    |   `-- append/link destination checkpoint; source history remains unchanged
    |-- move
    |   |-- preserve IDs where destination has no collision
    |   |-- remove selected source placements and content no longer used there
